# Frontend data flow

```text
@default/types → @default/api → @default/hooks → features|widgets|entities UI
```

## Rules

- Nest API reads/writes from UI go through `@default/hooks` (React Query).
- `@default/api` owns HTTP + query-keys; parse with `@default/types` Zod where applicable.
- **Forbidden** in `features/**` and `widgets/**`: `axios`, raw `fetch` to Nest/BFF for domain APIs, new local `api.ts` clients.
- Entities may keep thin UI/model helpers; data hooks live in `@default/hooks`.
- UI-only form state hooks may stay in the feature (`useLoginForm`).

## BFF (Next app only)

- Cookie auth and proxy: `frontend/app/api/auth/*`, `frontend/app/api/backend/*`, `frontend/src/shared/lib/bff-*`
- Do not move cookie/CSRF handling into `@default/api`; inject `baseURL` and refresh from the app.

## Public SSR

- Server Components may use `@default/api` server client or a small `public-server` helper that wraps it — not ad-hoc `fetch` scattered in features.

```text
✅ import { useUsers } from '@default/hooks'
✅ import { createApiClient } from '@default/api'
❌ features/users/api/client.ts with axios
❌ widgets → fetch('/api/backend/...')
```
